{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '397,587p' .task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md\"","aggregated_output":"### 6.3 Exact network fetch and ref flows\n\nAll fetches use a direct validated URL, a fresh private repository, one\nmanager-chosen destination under `refs/curator/`, and this exact common shape:\n\n```json\n[\n  \"<absolute-trusted-git>\",\n  \"--git-dir=<operation-private>/repo.git\",\n  \"--no-replace-objects\",\n  \"--no-lazy-fetch\",\n  \"--no-optional-locks\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"protocol.allow=never\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"protocol.<https-or-ssh>.allow=always\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"protocol.version=0\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"credential.helper=\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"core.askPass=<manager-broker>\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"core.hooksPath=<operation-private>/empty-hooks\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"core.fsmonitor=false\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"core.untrackedCache=false\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"submodule.recurse=false\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"fetch.recurseSubmodules=false\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"maintenance.auto=false\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"fetch.writeCommitGraph=false\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"fetch.fsckObjects=true\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"transfer.fsckObjects=true\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"http.followRedirects=false\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"http.sslVerify=true\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"http.proxy=\",\n  \"-c\",\n  \"https.proxy=\",\n  \"fetch\",\n  \"--quiet\",\n  \"--atomic\",\n  \"--no-tags\",\n  \"--no-recurse-submodules\",\n  \"--no-auto-maintenance\",\n  \"--no-write-fetch-head\",\n  \"--no-write-commit-graph\",\n  \"--refmap=\",\n  \"--jobs=1\",\n  \"--upload-pack=git-upload-pack\",\n  \"--\",\n  \"<validated-url>\",\n  \"<one-manager-refspec>\"\n]\n```\n\nThe selected transport is the only `protocol.*.allow=always` entry; the other\ntransport and every remote-helper protocol remain denied. There is no\n`--filter`, `--server-option`, remote name, configured refspec, stdin refspec,\nprune, mirror, depth/shallow option, tag auto-follow, or package-selected\nargument. Top-level `git fetch` receives closed stdin and bounded captured\ndiagnostics.\n\nThe one refspec is selected as follows:\n\n1. **Unsubstituted declaration without `tag`:**\n   Fetch `<full-locked-oid>:refs/curator/locked`. A full hexadecimal object\n   name is the only non-ref source admitted. On success, manager code still\n   parses and recomputes that object and requires a commit. A nonzero fetch is\n   `build_repository_source_unavailable`. There is no tag, branch, advertised\n   ref, or all-refs fallback.\n2. **Unsubstituted declaration with `tag`:**\n   Always fetch\n   `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/curator/tag` as the sole acquisition attempt. The\n   manager MUST NOT first or later fetch `<full-locked-oid>`, even when the\n   server permits direct object-ID wants. Manager code requires exactly the\n   fixed destination ref, parses and recomputes a lightweight or annotated-tag\n   chain with section 6.6.2's common grammar, and requires the terminal object\n   to be a commit exactly equal to `locked_commit.hex`. A different terminal\n   commit is `build_repository_ref_moved`. A missing exact ref, nonzero fetch,\n   or transport failure is `build_repository_source_unavailable`. A malformed\n   or incomplete fetched object graph retains the section 6.6 stable semantic\n   or incomplete-source error. There is no direct-object, branch, all-tags, or\n   alternate-ref fallback.\n3. **Operator network substitution:**  \n   A full `revision` fetches\n   `<full-oid>:refs/curator/effective`; a `tag` fetches\n   `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/curator/effective`; a `branch` fetches\n   `refs/heads/<branch>:refs/curator/effective`. There is no fallback between\n   forms. The declared repository lock's object format initializes the private\n   repository and MUST match the substituted remote; the manager never retries\n   under another hash family. The exact resulting commit becomes the effective\n   receipt identity.\n\nEvery destination is fixed manager namespace text; remote data cannot choose a\nlocal ref, refmap, refspec, helper, upload-pack, filter, or server option.\n`FETCH_HEAD`, remote-tracking refs, local heads/tags, commit-graphs, and\nmaintenance state MUST remain absent. A nonzero fetch, unexpected local ref,\nunexpected child, or any write outside the private repository fails and\ndiscards the attempt.\n\nFor an unsubstituted tagged source, exact-tag fetch and terminal-lock equality\nare preconditions of source resolution. They run before source audit can\nsucceed, before artifact-cache lookup, and before any compiler child. A failure\npublishes no snapshot, audit success, receipt, marker, or artifact. A\nsyntax-only offline check that cannot perform the exact-tag fetch emits only\n`build_repository_unverified_offline`; install, update, repair, and\ncoverage-claiming audit return `build_repository_source_unavailable` before\nmutation.\n\nThe conformance matrix is invariant to direct object-ID want policy because a\ntagged declaration never issues such a want:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"tag-match-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n    \"result\": \"source-resolved\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"tag-moved-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"89abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\",\n    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_ref_moved\",\n    \"audit_started\": false,\n    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n    \"compiler_started\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"tag-missing-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n    \"remote_ref_present\": false,\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_source_unavailable\",\n    \"audit_started\": false,\n    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n    \"compiler_started\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"tag-match-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n    \"result\": \"source-resolved\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"tag-moved-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"89abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\",\n    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_ref_moved\",\n    \"audit_started\": false,\n    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n    \"compiler_started\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"tag-missing-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n    \"remote_ref_present\": false,\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_source_unavailable\",\n    \"audit_started\": false,\n    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n    \"compiler_started\": false\n  }\n]\n```\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
