losure resolution\nprotocol/core.md:702:## 8. Content hashes\nprotocol/core.md:717:### 8.1 Build-source identity\nprotocol/core.md:746:### 8.2 Go toolchain identity\nprotocol/core.md:786:## 9. Compiled-artifact cache and receipts\nprotocol/core.md:788:### 9.1 Local `go-v1` receipt schema 1\nprotocol/core.md:834:### 9.2 External `go-repository-v1` receipt schema 2\nprotocol/core.md:873:### 9.3 Shared protected-cache rules\nprotocol/core.md:919:## 10. Install markers\nprotocol/core.md:1002:## 11. Adapter ledger\nprotocol/core.md:1010:## 12. External build publication and closed extensions\nprotocol/core.md:1012:### 12.1 Publication, shims, and rollback\nprotocol/core.md:1032:### 12.2 Operator credentials and signing\nprotocol/core.md:1049:### 12.3 Future closed-driver admission\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:1:# Decision 0005: external build repositories\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:3:## Context\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:21:## Decision\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:23:### Version boundary\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:36:### Manifest and descriptor ownership\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:61:### Declared and effective source\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:104:### Raw snapshot and audit boundary\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:150:### Receipt, marker, status, and lifecycle\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:185:### Credential, signing, and future-driver ownership\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:211:## Stable failure classes\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:236:## Rejected alternatives\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:257:## Compatibility impact\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:265:## Security impact\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'network substitution|Protected external snapshot|snapshot key|Garbage collection|allowlist|revocation|tag-lock|artifact-cache|compiler work|effective repository object format|declared repository' protocol/core.md SECURITY.md decisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md\"","aggregated_output":"decisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:132:Before any artifact-cache lookup or compiler child, including on a claimed\nSECURITY.md:30:The protocol provides integrity, provenance, revocation, rollback detection,\nSECURITY.md:178:Before an artifact-cache lookup or compiler child, the manager MUST freeze and\nprotocol/core.md:332:The command MUST select exactly one declared repository and exactly one target\nprotocol/core.md:335:mismatched driver MUST fail before artifact-cache lookup or compiler execution\nprotocol/core.md:473:not `h/a-evil`. An empty allowlist permits all network identities. Local\nprotocol/core.md:474:sources bypass the network allowlist.\nprotocol/core.md:526:operator network substitution MUST use exactly one structured ref:\nprotocol/core.md:586:A network substitution uses the same canonical identity and transport grammar\nprotocol/core.md:660:immutable regular-file snapshot. Before audit success, artifact-cache lookup,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
