{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'task-board resource --help'","aggregated_output":"Manage attached resources such as screenshots, docs, logs, and other files.\n\nUse \"task-board resource add\" to create a new attached resource, \"task-board\nresource update\" to replace an existing one, \"task-board resource delete\" to\nremove it, and \"task-board resource get\" to materialize a resource back to the\nlocal filesystem for inspection.\n\nUsage:\n  task-board resource [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  add         Attach a new file resource to an element\n  delete      Delete a resource from an element (requires --confirm)\n  get         Download a resource to the local filesystem\n  update      Replace an existing file resource on an element\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for resource\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --board-dir string      Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \".task-board\")\n      --insecure              Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\n      --json                  Output in JSON format\n      --no-update-check       Disable automatic update check\n      --remote string         Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\n      --remote-board string   Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\n\nUse \"task-board resource [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
